{
  "dom_id": "step-q355394",
  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "Let $g(y)$ be a profit for product $y,$ where $y\\in \\{3,7,11,15\\}.$ We want to write the best product $\\overset{^}{y}$ as \"the value of $y$ that makes $g(y)$ as large as possible.\"\n\nWhich of the following correctly defines $\\overset{^}{y}?$",
  "worked_solution": "We want $\\overset{^}{y}$ to be an *input value* $y$ where the profit $g(y)$ is as large as possible. \n\nThat is exactly what $\\operatorname{arg}⁡max$ returns.\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{y}=\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{y\\in \\{3,7,11,15\\}}g(y).\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
